# 🟢 LAB 1 – Create Basic VNet

---

## Step 1 – Create Resource Group

```bash
az group create \
  --name rg-vnet-lab \
  --location centralindia
```

---

## Step 2 – Create VNet with Public & Private Subnets

```bash
az network vnet create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --name vnet-lab \
  --address-prefix 10.10.0.0/16 \
  --subnet-name public-subnet \
  --subnet-prefix 10.10.1.0/24
```

Add private subnet:

```bash
az network vnet subnet create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --vnet-name vnet-lab \
  --name private-subnet \
  --address-prefix 10.10.2.0/24
```

---

# 🟢 LAB 2 – Deploy Public VM (Web Tier)

Equivalent to public EC2.

```bash
az vm create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --name vm-public \
  --image Ubuntu2204 \
  --size Standard_B1s \
  --vnet-name vnet-lab \
  --subnet public-subnet \
  --admin-username azureuser \
  --generate-ssh-keys
```

Check public IP:

```bash
az vm list-ip-addresses -g rg-vnet-lab -n vm-public
```

---

# 🟢 LAB 3 – Deploy Private VM (Backend)

No public IP.

```bash
az vm create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --name vm-private \
  --image Ubuntu2204 \
  --size Standard_B1s \
  --vnet-name vnet-lab \
  --subnet private-subnet \
  --public-ip-address "" \
  --admin-username azureuser \
  --generate-ssh-keys
```

---

# 🟢 LAB 4 – Network Security Group

---

## Create NSG

```bash
az network nsg create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --name nsg-public
```

Allow SSH:

```bash
az network nsg rule create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --nsg-name nsg-public \
  --name allow-ssh \
  --priority 100 \
  --direction Inbound \
  --access Allow \
  --protocol Tcp \
  --destination-port-range 22
```

Attach to subnet:

```bash
az network vnet subnet update \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --vnet-name vnet-lab \
  --name public-subnet \
  --network-security-group nsg-public
```

---

# 🟢 LAB 5 – Route Table (UDR)

Simulate firewall scenario.

```bash
az network route-table create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --name rt-private
```

Add route blocking internet:

```bash
az network route-table route create \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --route-table-name rt-private \
  --name block-internet \
  --address-prefix 0.0.0.0/0 \
  --next-hop-type None
```

Attach:

```bash
az network vnet subnet update \
  --resource-group rg-vnet-lab \
  --vnet-name vnet-lab \
  --name private-subnet \
  --route-table rt-private
```

Now private subnet has no internet access.

